The '''Utero''' is an alternate floor to the {{s|Womb}}. Unlike other alternate floors, the Utero does not need to be unlocked, aside from unlocking the Womb. While the theme of Utero overlaps heavily with the Womb, it appears to emphasize gore and disfigurement rather than its counterpart's focus on 'intact' viscera, though the difference in enemy make-up is still more subtle compared to other floors nonetheless. Its walls are slightly different, with white ribs spaced out on the walls, and the floor contains several new enemies that are bloodier and more deformed, as well as more enemies borrowed from later chapters, such as the {{s|Cathedral}} and {{s|Sheol}}, such as Holy Leeches or Bloodshot Eyes.

Like the Womb, from this floor onward, {{r|Treasure Room}}s and {{r|Shop}}s will no longer naturally generate and all damage that is taken deducts a full heart from Isaac's HP (unless he has {{i|The Wafer}}), regardless of the source.

{{dlc|r}} While in the Utero, a dark yellowish desaturated screen shader and a warping effect will be applied to the screen, making it appear as if the area is submerged in fluid and further distinguishing the floor's appearance from the Womb.

