== Music ==
* {{dlc|nr}} The [[music]] for the Utero is titled ''Viscera''. The term “viscera” refers to the internal organs in the body. The {{s|Womb}} shares this same track, making Utero the only floor in base Rebirth which does not have its own track.<ref name="music">[https://ridiculon.bandcamp.com/album/the-binding-of-isaac-rebirth-ost Binding of Isaac: Rebirth OST]</ref>
* {{dlc|r}} The [[music]] for the Utero is titled ''Caesarian''. A caesarian is a medical procedure where a baby is surgically removed from the mother due to complications during birth.<ref name="music"/>
* The music heard during the fight against Mom's Heart/It Lives! is called ''Ventricide''. Ventricide combines ventricle, a word that means a hollow area in an organ and is often associated with the heart, and the suffix -cide, which denotes the act of killing.

== Trivia ==
* ''Utero'' is the ablative or dative form for the Latin word and medical term "uterus", meaning "womb", and it probably stands for the expression ''in utero'', "within the womb", which refers to certain surgical procedures or other occurrences taking place inside the womb or during the length of time that a fetus is in the uterus of the pregnant female.
* The Utero's backdrop (red walls with white ribs) was also the backdrop of the {{s|Womb}} in flash Isaac, as both floors looked exactly the same in flash Isaac.

